{
  "account": "plur",
  "background": {"color": "#0A0A0A"},
  "slides": [
    {
      "type": "cover",
      "main": ["SOURCE DIRECT"],
      "sub": "Nobody knew their faces. Nobody needed to."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Midnight sessions.",
        "Age 14.",
        "",
        "Two teenagers from St Albans —",
        "a quiet town an hour outside London —",
        "booked studio time at Hackney's Panic Studio.",
        "",
        "Midnight, because the rates dropped.",
        "",
        "Nobody was watching."
      ],
      "sub": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "They built a studio at home.",
        "",
        "By 17, they were pressing records.",
        "",
        "No press photos.",
        "No interviews.",
        "No biography.",
        "",
        "Just the music, moving through record shops",
        "in white sleeves."
      ],
      "sub": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "\"The Crane\" — 1996.",
        "",
        "The sample: Laputa, Castle in the Sky.",
        "A Japanese animation —",
        "a lost city floating above the clouds.",
        "",
        "A dark bassline. Broken beats.",
        "Something that felt like falling",
        "and floating at once.",
        "",
        "One of the most played records",
        "at the Metalheadz Sunday Sessions."
      ],
      "sub": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "\"The Cult\" landed on Metalheadz.",
        "\"A Made Up Sound\" became a darkside classic.",
        "",
        "These were not pop records.",
        "",
        "They were for the people who stood",
        "at the back of the room",
        "and closed their eyes."
      ],
      "sub": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Their sound lived between two worlds.",
        "",
        "LTJ Bukem's light — atmospheric, wide.",
        "Photek's precision — cold, surgical.",
        "",
        "Source Direct never fully chose a side.",
        "",
        "Sweeping minor-key melodies",
        "over sharp, splintered breaks.",
        "",
        "That tension is why the tracks still hold."
      ],
      "sub": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "\"Exorcise the Demons\" — their only album.",
        "1999. Virgin Records.",
        "",
        "Fact Magazine: #96",
        "in the 100 best albums of the 1990s.",
        "",
        "That same year, Phil Aslett left.",
        "No explanation. Just gone.",
        "",
        "Jim Baker continued alone",
        "under the same name."
      ],
      "sub": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "cta",
      "text": [
        "The Crane was reissued in 2016.",
        "",
        "It still sounds like something",
        "that hasn't happened yet."
      ],
      "strobe": "SOURCE DIRECT",
      "cta": "Save this. You'll need it."
    }
  ]
}
